            "review_title": "Review at Back Fire Bar & Cafe",
            "review_text": "Frank F\nUtrecht, The Netherlands22 contributions\n1\nBurger raw in the middle, bland, overpriced for what you get\nMar 2019 • Couples\nWent here with my wife during lunchtime. We shared a tea and an 'American beef burger'. Well, that one didn't deserve the name at all.\nBut I'll start with the positive: you get a good portion of a burger with a small portion of fries. \n\nUnfortunately it stopped there. Complete lack of seasoning, an absence of freshness and flavours. Tasteless bread, cheap onions and Vietnamese style gherkins that were completely bland, cheese tasted mushy and bland, a piece of bacon you're happy to see only to be let down by how poorly it's done (was closer to cooked ham). No flavour in anything and to make it worse no sauce and about half of the beef was undercooked/raw in the middle.\n\nTalked to the waiter about the raw beef. We were offered some bread with butter, nice gesture but hardly enough and not what we came for. Paid full price for the risk of getting sick and a half-finished bland burger. No thanks\nRead more\nReview collected in partnership with this restaurant \nWritten March 21, 2019",
